From f01d709f743c44db96fdb5d73a613c63a88c539b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NNdroid <99177648+NNdroid@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:28:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] pon: local ONU identity tooling and a one-shot line re-open

Collapse the fork-only commits on top of pbs05/openwrt-pon-userspace into a single delta. Only the fork delta changes: the resulting tree is identical to the pre-squash tip, and the intermediate revert pair that cancelled itself out is gone.

- luci-app-pon: report the CTC ONU serial number and the LOID bytes actually sent on the wire, expose the LOID padding on either side of the field, and allow the PON MAC to be overridden.
- airoha-pon-daemons: thread those identity overrides through the OAM and OMCI configuration and fill the 24-byte LOID field through one helper so the reported and transmitted bytes cannot disagree.
- airoha-ponctl: add /etc/init.d/pon-reopen, a one-shot service that re-opens the line once after boot when the EPON front end comes up dark.
